---
term: Delegation of functions
section: principles
order: 10
definition: The practice of delegating each function that a charter's articles define, such as measurement, optimization, or processing, to its own commission of the charter, so that no commission can judge or rewrite its own work.
seeAlso:
  - constitutional-authority
  - executive-agent
  - measurement-mechanism
---
Each delegated function is a commission of the charter. Whoever holds [[constitutional authority]] keeps it and doesn't delegate it.

The Social Charter also separates three questions that conventional elections bundle together:

- Who or what is legitimately represented
- What objective to pursue
- Who executes it

Separating these questions unbundles electoral legitimacy from administrative competence. In a democratic charter, members can revise their charter while delegating implementation to professional administrators or AI.
